# pi-mounts.conf — additional volumes for the pi-agent service.
# One mount per line, compose volume syntax:
#   HOST_PATH:CONTAINER_PATH[:OPTIONS]
# HOST_PATH: absolute, or starting with ~ (expanded to $HOME).
# OPTIONS: standard docker/podman volume flags, comma-separated
#          (ro, rw, Z, z, ...). Omit for rw (add Z manually on Podman/SELinux
#          if the target is not already covered by compose.yaml's defaults).
#
# Rendered into compose.mounts.override.yaml by `pi-ramalama --render-mounts`,
# which `ensure_environment` calls automatically. MUST be current — and the
# resulting container MUST be (re)started — before running
# `pi-ramalama --install-extensions`, otherwise extension installers writing
# to a path listed here will write into the container's ephemeral layer
# instead (shadowed once the real mount is added later).
#
# Core mounts (pi-agent home dirs, settings.json, extensions volume) are
# already defined in compose.yaml — do not duplicate them here. Use this
# file only for additional, host-specific, or optional mounts (extra skill
# packs, extension source trees you're developing against, shared caches).

# Example:
# ~/.config/cortexkit:/root/.config/cortexkit:Z

